{
  "title": "Posterior Labral Tear",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3057/posterior-labral-tear",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 17 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A posterior labral tear is referred to as a reverse Bankart lesion, or attenuation of the posterior capsulolabral complex, and commonly occurs due to repetitive microtrauma in athletes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with positive posterior labral provocative tests and confirmed with MRI studies of the shoulder.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be nonoperative or operative depending on chronicity of symptoms, degree of instability, and patient activity demands.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "athletes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**weightlifters** (bench press)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**football linemen** (blocking)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "swimmers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gymnasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "wrestlers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**repetitive microtrauma** to the posterior capsulolabral complex",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common mechanism",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "posteriorly directed force with the arm in a flexed, internally rotated and adducted position",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "glenoid retroversion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patients with increased glenoid retroversion (~17°) were 6x more likely to experience posterior instability compared to those with less glenoid retroversion (~7°)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Kim lesion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "an **incomplete and sometimes concealed avulsion of posteroinferior labrum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Posterior labrum",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "function",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "helps generate cavity-compression effect of glenohumeral joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "creates 50% of the glenoid socket depth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**provides posterior stability**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "anatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "composed of fibrocartilagenous tissue",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**anchors posterior inferior glenohumeral ligament (PIGHL)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Glenohumeral joint anatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**vague, nonspecific posterior shoulder pain** is the most common symptoms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "worsens with provocative activities that apply a posteriorly directed force to the shoulder",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ex: pushing heavy doors, bench press, push-ups",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**clicking** or **popping** in the shoulder with range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sense of instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "less common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pain during throwing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "late cocking phase",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior joint line tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**posterior apprehension test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "arm positioned with shoulder forward flexed 90° and adducted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "apply anterior support to scapula",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "apply posteriorly directed force to shoulder through humerus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "positive if patient experiences sense of instability or pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posterior load and shift test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patient rests arm at their side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "grasp the proximal humerus and apply a posteriorly directed force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "assess distance of translation and patient response",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "grade 0 = no translation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "grade 1 = to edge of glenoid",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "grade 2 = over edge of glenoid but spontaneously relocates",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "grade 3 = over edge of glenoid, does not spontaneously relocate",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**jerk test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "arm positioned with shoulder abducted 90° and fully internally rotated",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "axially load humerus while adducting the arm across the body",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**clunk** indicates subluxation of the humeral head off the posterior glenoid",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "highly sensitive and specific for a **posterior labral tear**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**kim test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "arm positioned with shoulder abducted 90° and forward flexed 45°",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "apply posteriorly and inferiorly directed force to shoulder through humerus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "positive if patient experiences pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "highly sensitive and specific for **posteroinferior labral tear**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "true AP, scapular Y and axillary views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**axillary view required** to ensure glenohumeral joint reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "posterior shoulder dislocations may be missed on AP radiographs alone",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often normal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in chronic cases axillary view may show",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**glenoid retroversion** or",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**posterior glenoid erosion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3057/images/tear.jpg",
              "caption": "posterior labral tear"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "diagnostic study of choice",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**technique**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**intra-articular contrast** increases sensitivity for labral pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification, NSAIDs, PT",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "rotator cuff and deltoid strengthening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "periscapular stabilization",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior labral repair, capsulorrhaphy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "extensive nonoperative management fails",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "arthroscopic and open techniques may be used",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**arthroscopic** preferred to open given the extensive posterior surgical dissection required",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "more reliable return to play",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**suture anchor repair and capsulorrhaphy results in fewer recurrences and revisions than non-anchored repairs**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**probing of posterior labrum** is required to rule out a subtle Kim lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "generally good",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "return to previous level of function in overhead throwing athletes not as reproducible as other athletes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "failure risk increases if adduction and internal rotation are not avoided in the acute postoperative period",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "increased risk of recurrence if posterior bone loss is not addressed concurrently",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "recent studies show 11% glenoid bone loss resulted in a 10.4 times statistically higher surgical failure rate, while a 15% bone loss resulted in a 24.4 times statistically higher failure rate",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Axillary nerve palsy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior branch of the axillary nerve is at risk during arthroscopic stabilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "travels within 1 mm of the inferior shoulder capsule and glenoid rim",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "at risk during suture passage at the posterior inferior glenoid",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Overtightening of posterior capsule**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can lead to anterior subluxation or coracoid impingement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
